      "body": "Thank you for your great work. I am running on a cloud server and unable to start carla. Even after `apt install vulkan-tools` and `apt install libgeos-dev`.\nSystem: Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS GPU info: NVIDIA 4090 Driver Version: 530.41.03 CUDA Version: 12.1. Carla version: 0.9.15 and 0.9.16.\nI try to start Carla with `./CarlaUE4.sh -RenderOffScreen -nosound -fps=10 -carla-rpc-port=2000`\n\nHowever I get output like that after stuck 60s:\n```\n$ ./CarlaUE4.sh -RenderOffScreen -nosound -fps=10 -carla-rpc-port=2000\nchmod: changing permissions of '/mnt/evad_fs/worldmodel/zhoujiawei/carla-0.9.15/CarlaUE4/Binaries/Linux/CarlaUE4-Linux-Shipping': Operation not permitted\n4.26.2-0+++UE4+Release-4.26 522 0\nDisabling core dumps.\nsh: line 1: xdg-user-dir: command not found\nLowLevelFatalError [File:Unknown] [Line: 1214] \nGameThread timed out waiting for RenderThread after 60.00 secs\nSignal 11 caught.\nMalloc Size=65538 LargeMemoryPoolOffset=65554 \nCommonUnixCrashHandler: Signal=11\nEngine crash handling finished; re-raising signal 11 for the default handler. Good bye.\n./CarlaUE4.sh: line 5: 104765 Segmentation fault      (core dumped) \"$UE4_PROJECT_ROOT/CarlaUE4/Binaries/Linux/CarlaUE4-Linux-Shipping\" CarlaUE4 \"$@\"\n```\n\n#151 has the same issues and [here](https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/Bench2Drive/issues/151#issuecomment-2970074301) has a solution. However, as I want to use carla in the cloud server, I must start Carla in the contraner. Any ideas or advice on how to solve this? I would really appreciate it.\n",
